## https://github.com/tj/git-extras/blob/main/Commands.md
Git Extras: Abort current revert,rebase,merge or cherry-pick,without the need to find exact command in history           | git abort
Git Extras: Define,search and show aliases                                                                               | git alias
Git Extras: Creates a zip archive of the current git repository                                                          | git archive-file
Git Extras: Populates the file matching authors/contributors -i with the authors of commits                              | git authors
Git Extras: Opens the current git repository website in your default web browser                                         | git browse
Git Extras: Opens the current git repository CI website in your default web browser.                                     | git browse-ci
Git Extras: Operations that execute on multiple git repositories                                                         | git bulk
Git Extras: Pretty listing of branches sorted by the date of their last commit                                           | git brv
Git Extras: Generates a changelog from git(1) tags (annotated or lightweight) and commit messages                        | git changelog
Git Extras: Does a hard reset and deletes all untracked files from the working directory, including those in .gitignore  | git clear
Git Extras: Does a hard reset and deletes all untracked files from the working directory, excluding those in .gitignore  | git clear-soft
Git Extras: Add a co-author to the last commit                                                                           | git coauthor
Git Extras: List commits since date (defaults to "last week")                                                            | git commits-since
Git Extras: Continue current revert,rebase,merge or cherry-pick,without the need to find exact command in history        | git continue
Git Extras: Output author's contributions to a project                                                                   | git contrib
Git Extras: Output commit count                                                                                          | git count
Git Extras: Copy a file to another one keeping its history and allowing for merge conflicts handling                     | git cp
Git Extras: Create local branch name                                                                                     | git create-branch
Git Extras: Delete local and remote branch name                                                                          | git delete-branch
Git Extras: Deletes branches that are listed in git branch --merged                                                      | git delete-merged-branches
Git Extras: Deletes branches that have been "squashed-merged" into a specified branch                                    | git delete-squashed-branches
Git Extras: Delete submodule name                                                                                        | git delete-submodule
Git Extras: Delete local and remote tag name                                                                             | git delete-tag
Git Extras: Lists files that differ from another branch                                                                  | git delta
Git Extras: Displays "effort" statistics                                                                                 | git effort
Git Extras: The main git-extras command                                                                                  | git extras
Git Extras: Create/Merge the given feature branch name                                                                   | git feature
Git Extras: Reset its contents to a clone of the remote                                                                  | git force-clone
Git Extras: Fork the given github <repo>                                                                                 | git fork
Git Extras: Create empty local branch                                                                                    | git fresh-branch
Git Extras: Clone repository into a subdirectory of the configured path                                                  | git get
Git Extras: Sets up the gh-pages branch                                                                                  | git gh-pages
Git Extras: Merge commits from src-branch into dest-branch                                                               | git graft
Git Extras: Calculate the change in blame between two revisions                                                          | git guilt
Git Extras: Generate sample gitignore file from gitignore.io                                                             | git ignore-io
Git Extras: Too lazy to open up .gitignore                                                                               | git ignore
Git Extras: Show information about the repo                                                                              | git info
Git Extras: List all commits on the local branch that have not yet been sent to origin                                   | git local-commits
Git Extras: Lock a local file filename                                                                                   | git lock
Git Extras: List local locked files                                                                                      | git locked
Git Extras: Commits changes with a generated message                                                                     | git magic
Git Extras: Merge branch into                                                                                            | git merge-into
Git Extras: Merges two repository histories                                                                              | git merge-repo
Git Extras: Print out which commits are on one branch or the other but not both                                          | git missing
Git Extras: Checks out a merge request from GitLab                                                                       | git mr
Git Extras: Completely remove a file from the repository,including past commits and tags                                 | git obliterate
Git Extras: Sends commits to a pastebin site using pastebinit                                                            | git paste
Git Extras: Checks out a pull request from GitHub                                                                        | git pr
Git Extras: Rebase a branch on top of another using a merge commit and only one conflict handling                        | git psykorebase
Git Extras: Create pull request via commandline                                                                          | git pull-request
Git Extras: Rewrite history to change author's identity                                                                  | git reauthor
Git Extras: Given you have a patch that doesn't apply to the current HEAD                                                | git rebase-patch
Git Extras: Release commit with the given <tag> and other options                                                        | git release
Git Extras: Rename a branch locally,and sync to remote via git push                                                      | git rename-branch
Git Extras: Rename a file or directory and ensure Git recognizes the change                                              | git rename-file
Git Extras: Rename a tag (locally and remotely)                                                                          | git rename-tag
Git Extras: Rename a git remote regardless of name conflict                                                              | git rename-remote
Git Extras: Git read-eval-print-loop                                                                                     | git repl
Git Extras: Reset one file to HEAD or certain commit                                                                     | git reset-file
Git Extras: Show the path to root directory of git repo                                                                  | git root
Git Extras: A convenient way to copy files from the current working tree to the working directory of a remote repository | git scp/rscp
Git Extras: Run grep as directed but replace the given files with the pattern                                            | git sed
Git Extras: Set up a git repository (if one doesn't exist),add all files,and make an initial commit                      | git setup
Git Extras: Show all branches merged in to current HEAD                                                                  | git show-merged-branches
Git Extras: Show the decorated graph view of one liner summarized commits from all branches                              | git show-tree
Git Extras: Show all branches not merged in to current HEAD                                                              | git show-unmerged-branches
Git Extras: Stamp the last commit message                                                                                | git stamp
Git Extras: Merge commits from src-branch into the current branch as a single commit                                     | git squash
Git Extras: Recall what you did or find what someone else did in a given range of time                                   | git standup
Git Extras: Outputs a repo or path summary                                                                               | git summary
Git Extras: Sync local branch with its remote branch                                                                     | git sync
Git Extras: Call touch on the given file,and add it to the current index. One-step creation of new files                 | git touch
Git Extras: Remove the latest commit                                                                                     | git undo
Git Extras: Unlock a local file filename                                                                                 | git unlock
Git Extras: Change files modification time to their last commit date                                                     | git utimes
Git Extras: Undo a Work In Progress(WIP) commit and put all of those changes back into the working directory             | git unwip
Git Extras: Create a Work In Progress(WIP) commit,which will include all changes in the working directory                | git wip